  "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a drag performer with bold makeup and a leopard-print outfit, holding a microphone, set against a vibrant, colorful background. The text overlay reads: 'they want to be accepted for who they are, yet there aren't able to accept themselves for who they are.' The overall intent of the meme is to convey a message of self-acceptance and the struggle for self-love, particularly within the context of LGBTQ+ identity. The visual of the drag performer, often associated with gender expression and performance, is juxtaposed with the text to highlight the internal conflict between societal acceptance and personal self-acceptance. There is no toxicity present in this meme; it does not contain abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propaganda elements. The intent is reflective and empathetic, aiming to resonate with individuals who may struggle with self-acceptance, without targeting or disparaging any specific group.",
